9306	Managing content moderation workflows		none
9307	What is a content moderation workflow?		none
9308	On some sites, new content and content revisions need to be <em>moderated</em>. That is, they need to pass through several <em>states</em> before becoming visible to site visitors. The collection of states and the definition of the transitions between states is known as a <em>workflow</em>. For example, new content might start out in a <em>Draft</em> state, and then might need to pass through several <em>Review</em> states before it becomes <em>Published</em> on the live site.		none
9309	Overview of content moderation workflows		none
9310	The core Content Moderation module allows you to expand on core software's "unpublished" and "published" states for content. It allows you to have a published version that is live, but have a separate working copy that is undergoing review before it is published. This is achieved by using workflows to apply different states and transitions to entities as needed.		none
9311	The core Workflows module allows you to manage workflows with states and transitions.		none
9312	See the related topics listed below for specific tasks and background information.		none
9313	On-line documentation about Content Moderation		none
