9643	The contact form will always have <em>Subject</em> and <em>Message</em> fields. If you want to add more fields, follow the steps in @adding_fields_topic.		10.5.8
9651	Content (blocks, content items, etc.) can be written in English or another language, and can be translated into additional languages. See @content_structure_topic to learn more about content.		10.5.8
9652	Many configuration items also include text that can be translated. Default configuration provided by your site's software is provided in English; you can also download community-provided translations. See @config_overview_topic to learn more about configuration.		10.5.8
9650	Core media items include audio, images, documents, and videos. You can add other media types, such as social media posts, through the use of contributed modules. Media items may be files located in your site's file system, or remote items referenced by a URL. Media items are content entities, and they are divided into media types (which are entity sub-types); media types can have fields. See @content_structure_topic for more information on content entities and fields.		10.5.8
9661	Add an entity reference field to an entity sub-type; see @content_structure_topic for more information on entities and reference fields.		10.5.8
9663	Check the indexing status of the Help search page. If it is not fully indexed, see @cron_topic about how to run Cron until indexing is complete.		10.5.8
9664	In the future, you can click <em>Rebuild search index</em> on this page, or @cache_topic, in order to force help topic text to be reindexed for searching. This should be done whenever a module, theme, language, or string translation is updated.		10.5.8
